.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_STORE-FILE 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ossl_store-file
.Nd The store 'file' scheme loader
.Sh SYNOPSIS
#include <openssl/store.h>
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for the 'file' scheme is built into
.Qo Li libcrypto Qc .
Since files come in all kinds of formats and content types, the 'file'
scheme has its own layer of functionality called "file handlers", which
are used to try to decode diverse types of file contents.
.Pp
In case a file is formatted as PEM, each called file handler receives
the PEM name (everything following any
.Pf ' Qo Li -----BEGIN Qc
\&') as well as possible PEM headers, together with the decoded PEM
body.
Since PEM formatted files can contain more than one object, the file
handlers are called upon for each such object.
.Pp
If the file isn't determined to be formatted as PEM, the content is
loaded in raw form in its entirety and passed to the available file
handlers as is, with no PEM name or headers.
.Pp
Each file handler is expected to handle PEM and non-PEM content as
appropriate.
Some may refuse non-PEM content for the sake of determinism (for
example, there are keys out in the wild that are represented as an ASN.1
OCTET STRING. In raw form, it's not easily possible to distinguish those
from any other data coming as an ASN.1 OCTET STRING, so such keys would
naturally be accepted as PEM files only).
.Sh NOTES
When needed, the 'file' scheme loader will require a pass phrase by
using the
.Sy UI_METHOD
that was passed via
.Xr OSSL_STORE_open 3 .
This pass phrase is expected to be UTF-8 encoded, anything else will
give an undefined result.
The files made accessible through this loader are expected to be
standard compliant with regards to pass phrase encoding.
Files that aren't should be re-generated with a correctly encoded pass
phrase.
See
.Xr passphrase-encoding 7
for more information.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ossl_store 7 ,
.Xr passphrase-encoding 7
